<p>Compare puts two outfits side by side and tells you what they share and where they differ.</p>
<h2>Start a comparison</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Select one outfit, then hold <code>Shift</code> and click a second, or press <code>Space</code> on each. Press <code>C</code>, or choose Compare.</li>
  <li>While signed in to Roblox you can also compare an outfit against what you’re wearing now.</li>
</ol>
<h2>What you see</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Shared and unique items</strong>, and a similarity score.</li>
  <li><strong>Body differences:</strong> colours, scale and avatar type.</li>
  <li><strong>Cost differences:</strong> buy-now and resale kept separate, with unknown prices counted rather than guessed.</li>
  <li><strong>Slider:</strong> drag to wipe between the two renders.</li>
</ul>
<p>Try it in <a href="/#compare">the Compare scene</a> or in <a href="/#demo">the demo</a>: pick a profile with a few outfits, select two, and press Compare.</p>
